{
  "case_id": "2016-16-74",
  "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BLATT: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court:\nPension plans for religious non-profits have been exempt from ERISA for over 30 years, whether or not a church established the plan. And the contrary holding of the three courts below should be reversed for three reasons.\nFirst, the text does not require a church to establish benefit plans for someone else's employees.\nSecond, the government's consistent view, over three decades, has generated enormous reliance interest and warrants deference. And third, affirmance would resurrect the precise problems that everyone understood the 1980 amendment would fix."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Why? There was a provision that was proposed that would have done very clearly what you think this provision does now. And Congress didn't pass it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, still, Ms. Blatt, there is a -- you know, there would be a simple way of accomplishing what you think this provision accomplishes. You know, something along the lines of just saying any plan maintained by a church-affiliated organization is a church plan or something like that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: It's not the problem with your reading. This (C)(i) seems to be predominantly about principal-purpose organizations. And I think the Respondent suggests that you would like it to read -- as reproduced on page 27 of their brief, you would like it to say includes a plan maintained by an organization controlled by or associated with a church. But this provision seems to be giving authority to principal-purpose organizations and not to entities controlled by or associated."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, this is a tricky question, but is this the question that was decided by the courts of appeals and is it the question that we agreed to review?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: What are the limits of that proposition? I mean, I don't quite understand, you're saying because these three government agencies interpreted the statute one way, we shouldn't be more -- we should be inclined to interpret it that way?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Why should it be persuasive? I mean, you faulted, I think, the courts of appeals. You -- you described their opinions as thinly reasoned. But that DCM that started it all from the IRS is certainly thinly reasoned."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: My question is: What can you point to, to tell us that the IRS letters were an important part of the motivation for Congress to make this change?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0000-0008",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STEWART: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court:\nI'd like to first to pick up on a point that Ms. Blatt alluded to when she was describing the -- the history of the statute and its amendment. I think the statute in its current form is probably not the type of provision that Congress would draft if it were doing the whole thing in one fell swoop. But it's important to understand that the text of the -- the current provision is the combination of things that were done in 1974 and things that were done in 1980."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Sometimes when Congress enacts a definition, it's trying to clarify what the defined term really means."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Stewart, can I ask you about some of the Respondents' hypotheticals where they offer hypothetical statutes that are very similar in structure to this one?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: I mean, that would seem ridiculous, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But I think, in construing this provision, it may be helpful to look at page 24 of the government's brief which explains -- which kind of clarifies something that Ms. Blatt was referring to earlier"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Sometimes on the hook?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Can you -- can you tell me what provision of ERISA -- and I'll ask Mr. Feldman the same thing if I have the chance -- what provision of ERISA explains which entity, if any, is responsible for paying benefits if, for example, a defined benefit plan is unable to do that with the assets in the plan?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0001-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "to be Congress was just a little bit careless in leaving in \"established and maintained\" at the beginning."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But it -- but it led to -- but it led to hundreds of letters from the IRS. Is there -- is that an exaggeration or is that -- aren't there hundreds of IRS letters approving --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FELDMAN: I think the practical significance is Congress's purpose here -- and, again, I don't think this is in dispute, and there's no other purpose that's been suggested, was hands off the church. If a church is involved with a plan, we don't -- we don't -- we want to have -- leave them the freedom to be outside of ERISA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: -- your perspective, what is the practical significance of requiring that the -- excuse me -- plans be established by a church?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Mr. Feldman, why do you think -- I mean, I've -- I have read all your arguments about why the IRS letters are not entitled to deference."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0003-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Isn't that, in itself, evidence -- not the Skidmore deference -- but evidence that the agency believed that the answer was different than you're promoting right now?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0003-0001",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "These were ex parte letters. Every one of them, up until the last couple of years, was done on an ex parte basis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So I'm just going to start with the funding issue. The one thing that's pellucid about C is that the church does not have to fund C(i) plans because the statute explicitly allows the maintaining organization to fund it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United Church of Christ and Evangelical Lutheran Church of America",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0003-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The brief by the United Church of Christ and the Evangelical Lutheran Church of America. They explain that the centralization that an establishment requirement would impose is anathema to their religious beliefs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-74",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1ecc9b7c0288919a1a67972baacc465991e9c98cc42487a11aca07c37396400b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1ecc9b7c0288-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Case is submitted."
    },
